Your actions as a data furnisher infringe upon my right to privacy and constitute aggravated identity theft under 18 U.S. Code 1028A. This statute establishes that knowingly transferring, possessing, or using, without lawful authority, a means of identification of another person during and in relation to a felony violation enumerated in the statute, can result in a term of imprisonment of two years in addition to the punishment provided for the underlying felony. 

