Additionally, under Section 616 of the FCRA, credit reporting agencies and entities that furnish information to them, such as creditors, are required to take reasonable measures to ensure the accuracy and completeness of the information in a consumer 's credit report. In this case, it is clear that these fraudulent hard inquiries were not initiated by me and therefore are not accurate or complete.

I request that you investigate these fraudulent hard inquiries as soon as possible and remove them from my credit report within 30 days of receipt of this letter, as required by law. Failure to do so would be a violation of the FCRA, and may result in legal action and penalties under the law.

